From 4a820e72a941c5a26aa2ae198a2423b20d91233a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2025 15:46:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] PENDING: i2c: i2c-qcom-geni: Add async write support

For the camera use case, the client needs to send
control information for various sensors on different
GPIIs, which will be processed once the sync timer
arrives. The client does not want to wait for the actual
transfer completion. Currently, the I2C GENI driver and
framework support only synchronous data transfer. To
enable the CCU QUP client to queue write frames without
waiting for transfer completion, add asynchronous write
data transfer support to the I2C driver.

Change-Id: I50189925683eed8d67b195b800d8500ce9c9c1ca
Signed-off-by: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
